christoffel-symbol-of-the-second-kind-cc.conceptual_definition:
The Christoffel symbol of the second kind, denoted $\Gamma^ho_{
u\sigma}$, represents the components of the unique torsion-free, metric-compatible affine connection (the Levi-Civita connection). It specifies how basis tangent vectors $\partial_
u$ change when differentiated along coordinate direction $\partial_\sigma$, such that $
abla_{\partial_\sigma} \partial_
u = \Gamma^ho_{
u\sigma} \partial_ho$.

