u$ and $\sigma$. While it carries three tensor-like indices, it is not a true tensor; under general coordinate transformations $x^\mu 	o x'^\mu$, it transforms inhomogeneously due to the second partial derivatives of the coordinate map. The symmetric part $\Gamma^ho_{(
u\sigma)}$ encodes connection geometry without torsion, directly governing geodesic motion via $ rac{d^2 x^ho}{d	au^2} + \Gamma^ho_{
u\sigma}  rac{dx^
u}{d	au}  rac{dx^\sigma}{d	au} = 0$.
